\begin{array}{cl}
ax+3 & \text{ if }x>0, \\
ab & \text{ if }x=0, \\
bx+c & \text{ if }x<0.
\end{array}
\right.\] Given $f(2) = 5$, $f(0) = 5$, and $f(-2) = -10$, we can set up the following equations based on the conditions: \[f(2) = 2a + 3 = 5,\] \[f(0) = ab = 5,\] \[f(-2) = -2b + c = -10.\] We need to solve these equations for $a$, $b$, and $c$. From the first equation: \[2a + 3 = 5 \implies 2a = 2 \implies a = 1.\] From the second equation: \[ab = 5 \implies 1 \cdot b = 5 \implies b = 5.\] From the third equation: \[-2b + c = -10 \implies -2 \cdot 5 + c = -10 \implies -10 + c = -10 \implies c = 0.\] Therefore, $a = 1$, $b = 5$, and $c = 0$. The value of $a + b + c$ is $1 + 5 + 0 = 6$. </think> <answer> 6 </answer>

